        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of બરણી (barṇī) is not settled. CDIAL has no entry for it. DEDR lists Dravidian words for a jar or casket, such as Kannada and Tulu baraṇi, \"china jar\", and Tamil paraṇi, but no Gujarati word, so whether બરણી (barṇī) belongs with them is not known (DEDR 3954)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
